#### Problem 1: HTTP Timeout Failures for Long-Running Operations

**Scenario**: Provider credentialing API performs background checks taking 90-180 seconds:

```csharp
// Problematic synchronous implementation
[HttpPost("providers/credentialing")]
public async Task<IActionResult> SubmitCredentialingApplication(
    CredentialingApplication application)
{
    try
    {
        // Validate application (2-3 seconds)
        var validationResult = await _validator.ValidateAsync(application);
        if (!validationResult.IsValid)
            return BadRequest(validationResult.Errors);

        // Check state medical board license (30-45 seconds)
        var licenseCheck = await _stateLicensingService.VerifyLicenseAsync(
            application.LicenseNumber, application.State);

        // Query National Practitioner Data Bank (45-60 seconds)
        var npdbCheck = await _npdbService.QueryProviderAsync(
            application.Npi, application.TaxId);

        // Verify DEA registration if prescriber (20-30 seconds)
        var deaCheck = application.IsPrescriber
            ? await _deaService.VerifyRegistrationAsync(application.DeaNumber)
            : null;

        // Check professional liability insurance (15-20 seconds)
        var insuranceCheck = await _insuranceVerificationService.VerifyAsync(
            application.InsurancePolicyNumber);

        // Save credentialing results
        var credentialingId = await _repository.SaveAsync(new CredentialingRecord
        {
            ApplicationId = application.Id,
            LicenseStatus = licenseCheck.Status,
            NpdbStatus = npdbCheck.Status,
            DeaStatus = deaCheck?.Status,
            InsuranceStatus = insuranceCheck.Status
        });

        return Ok(new { CredentialingId = credentialingId });
    }
    catch (TaskCanceledException)
    {
        // Request timed out - but which check failed?
        // Backend processing may still be running!
        return StatusCode(408, "Request timeout");
    }
}
```

**Problems**:
- Total execution time substantially exceeds API Management timeout thresholds
- API Management timeout causes failure before backend processing completes
- Client receives timeout error even when backend processing completes successfully
- No way to retrieve results of timed-out requests
- Backend resources wasted on processing that clients can't access
- Retries duplicate expensive background checks

**Impact**:
- Provider onboarding SLA violations when applications timeout requiring manual intervention
- User frustration: providers must resubmit applications multiple times
- Increased background check costs due to duplicate processing from retries
- Compliance risk: incomplete audit trails when requests timeout mid-processing

