#### Problem 3: Poor Mobile User Experience

**Scenario**: Member app requests comprehensive health summary requiring federated query:

```javascript
// Mobile app code - React Native
const loadHealthSummary = async (memberId) => {
  setLoading(true);
  setLoadingMessage("Loading your health information...");

  try {
    // This call takes 45-90 seconds (HIE queries + claims aggregation)
    const response = await fetch(
      `${API_BASE}/members/${memberId}/health-summary`,
      {
        method: 'GET',
        timeout: 120000 // 2 minute timeout
      }
    );

    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error('Failed to load health summary');
    }

    const summary = await response.json();
    setHealthSummary(summary);
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.name === 'AbortError') {
      showError("Request timed out. Please try again.");
    } else {
      showError("Unable to load health summary");
    }
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
};
```

**Problems**:
- Mobile app frozen with loading spinner for 45-90 seconds
- User cannot navigate to other screens during loading
- Mobile network interruptions cause failure and require complete restart
- Battery drain from keeping HTTP connection active
- High user abandonment when loading exceeds acceptable thresholds
- No progress indication beyond generic "loading" message
- Screen locks on mobile devices disconnect connection, requiring restart

**User Experience Impact**:
- Poor app store ratings with frequent complaints about "slow" and "freezing"
- High session abandonment rate for health summary feature
- Elevated support tickets related to "app not responding" during report generation

