#### Problem 4: Batch Processing Without Status Tracking

**Scenario**: State agency uploads monthly enrollment file requiring processing:

```csharp
// Problematic synchronous batch processing
[HttpPost("eligibility/batch-upload")]
public async Task<IActionResult> ProcessEnrollmentFile(IFormFile file)
{
    // Validate file (1-2 seconds)
    if (file.Length > 100 * 1024 * 1024) // 100 MB
        return BadRequest("File too large");

    try
    {
        // Parse CSV file (30-60 seconds for large files)
        var enrollments = await _parser.ParseEnrollmentFileAsync(file);

        // Validate each enrollment (2-3 minutes)
        var validationResults = await _validator.ValidateBatchAsync(enrollments);

        // Process valid enrollments (5-10 minutes)
        var results = new List<EnrollmentResult>();
        foreach (var enrollment in validationResults.Valid)
        {
            var result = await _enrollmentService.ProcessAsync(enrollment);
            results.Add(result);
        }

        // Generate summary report (30-60 seconds)
        var summary = await _reportGenerator.GenerateBatchSummaryAsync(
            results, validationResults.Invalid);

        return Ok(summary);
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        // If processing fails at step 3, all work lost!
        return StatusCode(500, "Batch processing failed");
    }
}
```

**Problems**:
- Total processing time: 8-15 minutes for large enrollment files
- Exceeds all reasonable HTTP timeout thresholds
- Single failure loses all processing progress (no checkpointing)
- State agency user sees browser "loading" for 15 minutes with no progress indication
- No ability to retrieve partial results if processing interrupted
- Cannot prioritize urgent enrollments within batch
- Memory issues loading entire large record batch into memory

**Business Impact**:
- State contract SLA violations: "Enrollment file processing within 4 hours" missed due to repeated failures
- Manual intervention required: Operations team must run console apps outside API
- Poor state agency satisfaction scores related to file upload reliability

