#### Variation 3: Webhook with Retry and Circuit Breaker

**Description**: Enhanced webhook implementation with robust failure handling for unreliable client callback endpoints.

**Implementation**:
```csharp
public class WebhookDeliveryService
{
    private readonly IHttpClientFactory _httpClientFactory;
    private readonly ILogger<WebhookDeliveryService> _logger;

    public async Task DeliverWebhookAsync(string callbackUrl, WebhookPayload payload)
    {
        var policy = Policy
            .Handle<HttpRequestException>()
            .WaitAndRetryAsync(
                retryCount: 3,
                sleepDurationProvider: attempt => TimeSpan.FromSeconds(Math.Pow(2, attempt)),
                onRetry: (exception, timespan, attempt, context) =>
                {
                    _logger.LogWarning($"Webhook delivery attempt {attempt} failed: {exception.Message}");
                });

        try
        {
            await policy.ExecuteAsync(async () =>
            {
                var client = _httpClientFactory.CreateClient();
                client.Timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10);

                var content = new StringContent(
                    JsonSerializer.Serialize(payload),
                    Encoding.UTF8,
                    "application/json");

                // Add signature for webhook verification
                var signature = ComputeHmacSignature(payload);
                content.Headers.Add("X-Webhook-Signature", signature);

                var response = await client.PostAsync(callbackUrl, content);
                response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();

                _logger.LogInformation($"Webhook delivered successfully to {callbackUrl}");
            });
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError($"Webhook delivery failed after retries: {ex.Message}");
            // Store failed delivery for manual retry or dead-letter queue
            await _deadLetterQueue.EnqueueAsync(new FailedWebhook
            {
                CallbackUrl = callbackUrl,
                Payload = payload,
                Error = ex.Message
            });
        }
    }
}
```

**When to Use**: Server-to-server integrations where eventual notification delivery acceptable; partner APIs with known reliability issues

**Trade-offs**: Complex retry logic; requires dead-letter queue for permanently failed deliveries; webhook verification overhead

