#### HIPAA Compliance

**Access Control (§164.312(a))**:
- Operation status and results accessible only to requestor or authorized users
- Service-to-service authentication for background workers accessing PHI
- Authorization checks enforced on status and result endpoints
- Automatic account lockout after failed authentication attempts

**Audit Controls (§164.312(b))**:
```csharp
// HIPAA-compliant audit logging for async operations
public async Task<IActionResult> SubmitOperation(OperationRequest request)
{
    var operationId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

    // Log operation submission
    await _auditLogger.LogAsync(new AuditEvent
    {
        EventType = "AsyncOperationSubmitted",
        UserId = User.Identity.Name,
        OperationId = operationId,
        Timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow,
        IpAddress = HttpContext.Connection.RemoteIpAddress.ToString(),
        RequestData = SanitizeForAudit(request),
        DataElementsAccessed = DetermineDataElements(request)
    });

    // Operation processing...
}

// Log result retrieval
public async Task<IActionResult> GetOperationResult(string operationId)
{
    var result = await _resultStore.GetAsync(operationId);

    await _auditLogger.LogAsync(new AuditEvent
    {
        EventType = "AsyncOperationResultAccessed",
        UserId = User.Identity.Name,
        OperationId = operationId,
        Timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow,
        IpAddress = HttpContext.Connection.RemoteIpAddress.ToString(),
        AccessPurpose = "TreatmentPaymentOperations"
    });

    return Ok(result);
}
```

**Integrity Controls (§164.312(c))**:
- Operation status transitions validated (Accepted → Running → Completed/Failed)
- Result data checksums to detect tampering or corruption
- Message queue guarantees prevent message loss or duplication

**Transmission Security (§164.312(e))**:
- TLS 1.2+ enforced for all API endpoints (status, result retrieval)
- PHI encrypted at rest in status store and result store
- Message queue encryption in transit and at rest (Azure Service Bus encryption)
- Webhook delivery over HTTPS only; reject HTTP callback URLs

