### Real-World Example 3: State Enrollment Batch Processing

**Context**: State agencies upload monthly enrollment files requiring parsing, validation, and processing. Original synchronous implementation attempted to process entire file before returning, exceeding all timeout thresholds (8-15 minutes) and causing browser failures.

**Implementation**:

**File Upload Endpoint**:
```csharp
[HttpPost("eligibility/batch-upload")]
[RequestSizeLimit(100_000_000)]  // 100 MB
public async Task<IActionResult> UploadEnrollmentFile(
    IFormFile file,
    [FromQuery] string stateCode)
{
    // Quick validation
    if (file.Length > 100 * 1024 * 1024)
        return BadRequest("File exceeds 100 MB limit");

    if (!file.FileName.EndsWith(".csv"))
        return BadRequest("Only CSV files accepted");

    var operationId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

    // Upload file to blob storage
    var blobUrl = await _blobStorage.UploadAsync(
        containerName: "enrollment-uploads",
        blobName: $"{operationId}/{file.FileName}",
        content: file.OpenReadStream());

    // Create operation record
    await _operationStore.CreateAsync(new OperationStatus
    {
        OperationId = operationId,
        Status = OperationState.Accepted,
        CreatedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
        Requestor = User.Identity.Name,
        Metadata = new Dictionary<string, string>
        {
            ["FileName"] = file.FileName,
            ["FileSize"] = file.Length.ToString(),
            ["StateCode"] = stateCode,
            ["BlobUrl"] = blobUrl
        },
        ExpiresAt = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(7)
    });

    // Enqueue for processing
    await _serviceBus.SendMessageAsync("enrollment-processing", new ServiceBusMessage
    {
        MessageId = operationId,
        Body = BinaryData.FromString(JsonSerializer.Serialize(new
        {
            OperationId = operationId,
            BlobUrl = blobUrl,
            StateCode = stateCode
        }))
    });

    return Accepted(new
    {
        OperationId = operationId,
        StatusUrl = $"/api/operations/{operationId}",
        Message = "File uploaded successfully. Processing will begin shortly."
    });
}
```

**Background Batch Processor**:
```csharp
public class EnrollmentBatchProcessor
{
    public async Task ProcessBatchAsync(string operationId, string blobUrl, string stateCode)
    {
        await _operationStore.UpdateAsync(operationId, OperationState.Running, progress: 0);

        var results = new BatchProcessingResults();

        try
        {
            // Step 1: Parse file (10%)
            var enrollments = await ParseEnrollmentFileAsync(blobUrl);
            await _operationStore.UpdateProgressAsync(operationId, 10);

            // Step 2: Validate (30%)
            var validationResults = await ValidateBatchAsync(enrollments);
            await _operationStore.UpdateProgressAsync(operationId, 30);
            results.ValidationErrors = validationResults.Invalid;

            // Step 3: Process valid records (90%)
            var totalRecords = validationResults.Valid.Count;
            for (int i = 0; i < totalRecords; i++)
            {
                var enrollment = validationResults.Valid[i];

                try
                {
                    await _enrollmentService.ProcessAsync(enrollment);
                    results.SuccessCount++;
                }
                catch (Exception ex)
                {
                    results.Failures.Add(new FailureRecord
                    {
                        RecordNumber = i + 1,
                        MemberId = enrollment.MemberId,
                        Error = ex.Message
                    });
                }

                // Update progress every 100 records
                if (i % 100 == 0)
                {
                    var progress = 30 + (int)((i / (double)totalRecords) * 60);
                    await _operationStore.UpdateProgressAsync(operationId, progress);
                }
            }

            // Step 4: Generate summary report (100%)
            var report = await GenerateBatchSummaryAsync(results);
            await _resultStore.SaveAsync(operationId, report);
            await _operationStore.UpdateAsync(operationId, OperationState.Completed, progress: 100);

            // Send completion email to state user
            await _emailService.SendAsync(new Email
            {
                To = User.Identity.Name,
                Subject = $"Enrollment Batch Processing Complete - {stateCode}",
                Body = $"Processed {results.SuccessCount} enrollments. " +
                       $"View detailed report: {_baseUrl}/api/operations/{operationId}/result"
            });
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            await _operationStore.UpdateAsync(operationId, OperationState.Failed, error: new OperationError
            {
                Code = "BatchProcessingError",
                Message = ex.Message
            });
        }
    }
}
```

**Results**:
- **Upload acknowledgment**: Immediate (< 2 seconds) vs 8-15 minute timeout
- **User experience**: Upload and navigate away; email notification when complete
- **Processing reliability**: Near-complete success rate (vs frequent timeout failures)
- **Partial failure handling**: Individual record failures don't abort entire batch
- **Operational visibility**: Progress tracking enables better support
- **State satisfaction**: SLA compliance substantially improved
